  "raw_text": "289\n\n(Note/Nota: This is more formal language like what is found in Bible.\n \nYaban\n \n(3\nrd\n \nperson past tense of\n \nYabaia\n \n-\n \ngave\n)\n \nis\n\nmore common\n \nthan\n \nYan\n.\n \n/ Este es un lenguaje más formal como el que se encuentra en la Biblia.\n \nYaban\n \n(tiempo pasado\n\nen\n \n3\ner\n \npersona de\n \nYabaia\n \n-\n \ndado\n) es más común que\n \nYan\n.\n)\n\nYaram\n \n(v-2p-past/pasado-II)\n \n–\n \nyou gave, you allowed, you caused\n \n/ tu diste, tu permitiste, tu causaste\n\nYari\n \n(v-1p-past/pasado-II)\n \n–\n \nI gave, I allowed, I caused\n \n/ yo di, yo permiti, yo causé\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \ndb-Aiseya 38:17\n:\n \nyang saura yâri ba sut man pri ai sakram\n \n–\n \nall the bad (that) I caused, you freed (me from)\n \n/ todo\nlo malo (que) causé, me liberaste (de))\n\nYarka\n \n(a/t:\n \nYaka\n)\n \n–\n \nsomething given, something allowed, something arranged, something ordered\n \n/ algo dado,\nalgo permitido, algo arreglado, algo ordenado\n\nYas\n \n(v\n-\nimp)\n \n–\n \ngive, provide, allow, cause\n \n/ da,\n \nd\né\n, den,\n \nproporciona,\n \nproporcione, proporcionen,\n \npermit\ne\n,\n\npermita, permitan,\n \ncaus\na, cause, causen\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n: This is used as the imperative form for both\n \nYaia\n \nand\n \nYabaia\n \n–\n \nthere are no written examples of what would\n\nbe the form if following the rules of a regular verb: “\nYabs\n”\n \n/ Esto se usa como la forma imperativa tanto para\n \nYaia\n \ncomo\n\npara\n \nYabaia\n; no hay ejemplos escritos de cuál sería la forma si se siguen las reglas de un verbo regular: \"\nYabs\n\"\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\nintro\n):\n \nYas upla ba kaikbia Jehova wina lan takisa, man\n \nwina apia.\n \n–\n \nCause the person to look to learn from\n\nJehovah, not from you.\n \n/ Haga que la persona busque aprender de Jehová, no de usted.\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\n3\n):\n \nYas upla ba kau lan takan daukbia.\n \n–\n \nCause the person to desire to learn more.\n \n/ Hacer que la persona desee\n\naprender más.\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf21\n):\n \nMan Jehova ra puram sunma piua ra, yas bibikam witin mai walbia.\n \n–\n \nWhen you pray to Jehovah, let your\n\nbaby hear you.\n \n/\n \nCuando ore a Jehová, deje que su bebé lo escuche.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf23\n):\n \nYas luhpiam nani ba ai swira\n \nȃ\npu\n \nmai aisabia\n \n–\n \nLet your children to talk to you without shame\n \n/\n \nDeja que tus\n\nhijos te hablen sin vergüenza\n)\n\nYaka\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nYabaia/Yarka\n\nYakabaia\n \n(v-trans; instrans:\n \nYakawaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto pour, to dump, to disperse, to throw, to spread, to disseminate, to scatter\n \n/\nverter, volcar, dispersar, tirar, esparcir, diseminar, esparcir\n\nDipasta yakabaia pliska\n \n(\nbh73\n)\n \n–\n \ngarbage dump\n \n/ basurero\n\nYakabi aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto spread news\n \n/ difundir noticias\n\nYakabi lakaia\n \n(not in / no en:\n \ndict\n,\ndictu\n)\n \n–\n \nto distribute\n \n(\nbh19\n),\n \nto extend, to spread\n \n(\ndb-Aiseya 26:15\n) / distribuir\n(\nbh19\n), extender, difundir (\ndb-Aiseya 26:15\n)\n\nYakal\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \neagle\n \n/ águila\n\nYakan\n \n(adj ,n? , adv?)\n \n–\n \nalone\n \n/ solo\n\nYakan dara walaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto feel lonely\n \n/ sentirse solo\n\nYakan piua\n \n–\n \nprivate\n \ntime, time alone\n \n/ tiempo privado, tiempo a solas\n\nYakan swiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto leave alone\n \n/ dejar solo\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb89\n):\n \nMan nani sut naha tihmia yakan ai swima\n \n–\n \nYou all will leave me alone tonight\n \n/ Todos ustedes me dejarán\n\nen paz esta noche\n)\n\nYakan takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come to be alone\n \n/ estar solo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-11/19\n):\n \nDîa muni witin yakan takan daukras kan ki?\n \n–\n \nWhy was he not coming to be alone (isolating himself)?\n \n/\n¿Por qué no se estaba volviendo solo (aislándose)?)\n\nYakawaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nYakabaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto pour, to dump, to disperse, to throw, to spread, to disseminate, to scatter\n \n/\nverter, volcar, dispersar, tirar, esparcir, diseminar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-01/20\n):\n \nUpla nani ba dîa mâki kan ba swin bara plis sât sât ra plapi yakawan\n \n–\n \nThe people left what they were\nmaking and scattered, running to various places\n \n/ La gente dejó lo que estaban haciendo y se dispersó, corriendo a varios\nlugares)\n\nYakura\n \n–\n \nhigh, tall\n \n/ alto\n\nYalam\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncedar\n \n/ cedro\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\n1\n \nKing Nani\n \n5:6\n):\n \nLíbano ra blîks yalam dusa nani klakaia\n \n–\n \nSend to Lebanon to cut cedar trees\n \n/ Enviar a Líbano para\n\ncortar cedros\n)\n\nYama\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nYaia\n\nYamhpus\n \n(\ndb,dictu,fy\n;\n \nYahmpus\n-\ndict,my,sn\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nashes, powder\n \n/ cenizas, polvo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb\n20\n):\n \nYamhpus nani ba, tasba yuya sâtka kum ra ta\nu\nan\n \n–\n \nThe ashes turned into a sort of dust\n \n/ Las cenizas se convirtieron\n\nen un\n \ntipo\n \nde polvo\n)\n\nYamhpus mapla\n \n–\n \nash color\n \n/ color ceniza\n\nYami\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nheron\n \n/ garza",
